अत्ता तह रमणिज्जं अंहं गामस्स मंडणीहूअं,लुअतिलवाडिसरिच्छं सिसिरेणकअं भिसिणिसंडं	Look, mother-in-law! That lovely mass of lotuses Used to be the most beautiful thing in our village, But now winter has made them look Like a sesame field just after harvest
किं रुअसि ओणअमुही धवलाअंतेसु सालिछेत्तेसु,हरिआलमंडिअमुही णडि व्व सणवाडिआ जाआ	Cheer up! Don't cry for the paddy turning white. There's the field of hemp in bloom Like a dancer with her face painted yellow!
सहि एरिसि च्चिअ गई मा रुव्वसु तंसवलिअमुहअंदं,एआण वालवालुंकितंतुकुडिलाण पेम्माणं	Friend, this is just the way things happen— Stop your tears, don't turn your face away— Like the tendrils of a young cucumber, One's affections twine around an object That does not stay.
पाअपडिअस्स पइणो पुट्ठिं पुत्ते समारुहंतम्मि,दढमण्णुदूमिआइ विहासो घरिणीअ णिक्कंतो	When their little son Climbed on her husband's back As he knelt at her feet, She could not help laughing Despite her fierce anger.
रंधणकम्मणिउणिए मा जूरसु रत्तपाडलसुअंधं,मुहमारुअं पिअंतो धूमाइ सिही ण पज्जलइ	Don't get annoyed: There's nothing wrong with your cooking. That the fire won't burn but only smokes Is because it wants to inhale your breath That has the fragrance of red trumpetflowers.
घरिणीअ महाणसकम्मलग्गमसिमइलिएण हत्थेण,छित्तं मुहं हसिज्जइ चंदावत्थं गअं पइणा	The husband laughed at his wife's face Which, smudged with soot That stuck to her hand from kitchen work, Looked more than ever like the moon.
किं किं दे पडिहासइ सहीहि इअ पुच्छिआइ मुद्धाए,पढमुग्गअदोहलिणीअ णवर दइअं गआ दिट्ठी	When her friends asked the young wife Who was pregnant for the first time What she craved most She simply looked at her husband
अमअमअ गअणसेहर रअणीमुखतिलअ चंद दे छिवसु,छित्तो जेहि जिअअमो ममं पि तेहिं चिअ करेहिं	Sweet moon, Crest jewel of the sky, Beauty spot on the face of night, Touch me with the very same rays With which you've touched my most dearly beloved.
एहिज्ज सो पउत्थो अहअं कुप्पेज्ज सो वि अणुणेज्ज,इअ कस्स वि फलइ मणोरमाण माला पिअअमम्मि	First let my dear husband come home, Then let me give him a scolding, And then let him do his best to bring me round. There must be someone who can get all three wishes.
कोसंवकिसलवण्णअ तण्णअ उण्णामिएहि कण्णेहिं,हिअअट्ठिअं घरं वच्चमाण धवलत्तणं पाव	Young calf, Blushing red as a tender mango shoot, Running with ears pricked Towards the house of your desire, Assume the cool whiteness of a bull!
अलिअपसुत्तअ विणिमीलिअच्छ दे सुहअ मज्झ ओआसं,गंडपरिउं वणापुलइअंग ण पुणो चिराइस्सं	Dearest, I know you are not really asleep, Just keeping your eyes closed. I can see goose pimples rising as I kiss your cheek. I won't be late again.
असमत्त मंडण च्चिअ वच्च घरं से सकोउहल्लस्स,वोलाविअहलहलअस्स पुत्ति चित्ते ण लग्गिहिसि	Don't bother about your makeup, girl, Just go to him quickly, while he wants you. Once his longing is over He won't give you a thought.
आअरपणामिओट्टं अघडिअणासं असंहअणिडालं,वण्णघिअलित्तमुहिए तीए परिउंवणं भरिमो	I will never forget how, When her face was smeared with red ghee, We kissed, Carefully pouting our lips So that our noses and foreheads Wouldn't meet.
आणासआइ देंती तह सुरए हरिसविअसिअकवोला,गोसे वि ओणअमुही अह से त्ति पिअं ण सद्धहिमो	I refuse to believe that she who, Cheeks flushed with excitement, Is so demanding while making love Can really suit him, However meek she may be next mornin
पिअविरहो अप्पिअदंसणं च गरुआइ दो वि दुक्खाइ,जीअ तुमं कारिज्जसि तीअ णमो आहिजाईए	Being separated from what is dear And being forced to look at what isn't Are two causes of grief. I bow to your good breeding Which demands that you act as you do.
ण कुणंतो च्चिअ माणं णिसासु सुहसुत्तदरविवुद्धानं,सुण्णइअपासपरिमुसणवेअणं जइ सि जानंतो	You would not be so touchy If you knew the pain of falling asleep beside one's lover And waking up in the middle of the night To discover that the bed is empty.
णवलइपहरं अंगे जहिं जहिं महइ देअरो दाउं,रोमंच दंदराई तहिं तहिं दीसइ वहूए	At whichever part of her body Her husband's younger brother Aims the tender twig Gooseflesh raises a palisade of sticks.
अज्ज मए तेण विणा अणुहूअसुहाइ संभरंतीए,अहिणवमेहाण रवो णिसामिओ वज्झपडतो व्व	Today, As I think of the pleasures I've had Without him, The thunder of the first rain clouds Sounds like the executioner's drum.
णिक्किव जाआभीरुअ दुद्दंसण णिंवकीडसारिच्छ,गामो गामणिणंदण तुज्झ कए तह वितणुआइ	Headman's son, How heartless you are! Shying away from your wife You rarely show yourself, Like a worm in a neem berry. Yet because of you The whole village is pining away.
पहरवणमग्गविसमे जाआ किच्छेण लहइ से णिद्दं,गामणिउत्तस्स उरे पल्ली उण से सुहं सुअइ	Lying on his breast, Rough with the scars of many a wound, The headman's wife finds it difficult to rest, But his village sleeps sound.
अह संभाविअमग्गो सुहअ तुए च्चेअ णवर णिव्वूढो,एण्हिं हिअए अण्णं अण्णं वाआइ लोअस्स	What good old-fashioned honesty! But really, my dear, You're the only one who goes in for it. Nowadays people think one thing and say another.
उण्हाइ णीससंतो कीस मह परंमुहीअ सअणद्धे,हिअअं पलीविउं अणुसएण पुट्ठिं पलीवेसि	What do you think you are doing, Embracing me from behind? First you set fire to my heart And then you start burning my back With these hot sighs of remorse.
