सब्भावणे हभरिए रत्ते रज्जिज्जइ त्ति जुत्तम् इणं,अणहिअए उण हिअअं जं दिज्जइ तं जणो हसइ	To fall in love with a man who returns your love, One who is full of kindness and affection, Makes sense. But to give one's heart to a man who is utterly heartless Is laughable.
आरंभंतस्स धुअं लच्छी मरणं व होइ पुरिसस्स,तं मरणम् अणारंभे वि होइ लच्छी उण ण होइ	If a man shows initiative There is the prospect of either wealth or death. Even if he lacks initiative, death is certain, Wealth is not.
अक्खडइ पिआ हिअए अण्णं महिलाअणं रमंतस्स,दिट्ठे सरिसम्मि गुणे सरिसम्मि गुणे अईसंते	While making love to another woman His beloved will come to mind Both when he sees and doesn't see A familiar trait.
णइपूरसच्छहे जोव्वणम्मि अइपवसिएसुदिअहेसु,अणिअत्तासु अ राईसु पुत्ति किं दड्ढमाणेण	Silly girl, Youth races past Like a river in spate, The days are fleeting And the nights unreturning. So why this stubborn sulkiness?
कल्लं किर खरतिअओ पवसिहइ पिओ त्ति सुव्वइ जणम्मि,तह वड्ढ भअवइ णिसे जह से कल्लं चिअ ण होइ	Every one knows the hardhearted lover Leaves at dawn. Venerable Night, stretch on So that morning will not come.
होंतपहिअस्स जाआ आउच्छणजीअधारणरहस्सं,पुच्छंती भमइ घरं घरेण पिअविरहसहिरीओ	As her husband is about to depart She goes from door to door Asking all the women who suffer from absent husbands For the secret of surviving the farewell.
अण्णमहिलापसंगं दे देव्व करेसु अम्ह दइअस्स,पुरिसा एक्कंतरसा ण हु दोसगुणे विआणंति	O god, please Let my husband form other attachments, For men who have experience of one person only No longer appreciate what's good and what's bad.
थोअं पि ण णीइ इमा मज्झण्हे उअ सरीरतललुक्का,आअवभएण छाही वि ता पहिअ किं ण वीसमसी	Wayfarer, Your shadow is hiding beneath your body, Not showing one bit of itself for fear of the midday sun, So why don't you too take a rest?
सुहउच्छअं जणं दुल्लहं पि दूराहि अम्ह आणेंत,उअआरअ जर जीअं पि णेंत ण कआवराहोसि	By bringing that man Who keeps his distance To ask me how I'm feeling, You have proved a blessing. Now, fever, if you take my life, I will not complain.
आम जरो मे मंदो अहव ण मंदो जणस्स का तत्ती,सुहउच्छअ सुहअ सुअंधगंध मा गंधिरिं छिवसु	Why should anyone care Whether my fever has abated or not? You, my dear, asking how I am And smelling so fragrant, Do not touch me who stink of fever.
सिहिपिच्छलुलिअकेसे वेवंतोरु विणिमीलिअद्धच्छी,दरपुरिसाइनि विसमिरि जाणसु पुरिसाण जं दुक्खं	Your long hair sways like a peacock's fan, Your thighs quiver, your eyes half close, With long pauses you sort of play the man. Now do you see what hard work it is For a man?
पेम्मस्स विरोहिअसंधिअस्स पच्चक्खदिट्ठविलिअस्स,उअअस्स व ताविअसीअलस्स विरसो रसो होइ	Love Estranged and patched up again, Once its dissolution is plain to see, Will never taste right again Like water that has boiled then cooled
वज्जवडनाइरिक्कं पइणो सोऊण सिंजिणीघोसं,पुसिआइ करिमरीए सरिवंदीणं पि अच्छीइं	Thinking she hears the twang of her husband's bow Above the crashing thunder, The captive wife tells the royal hostages To wipe away their tears.
करिमरि अआलगज्जिरजलआसणिवडणपडिरवो एसो,पइणो धणुरव कंखिरि रोमंचं किं मुहा वहसि	It is only the echo of a thunderclap From an early rain cloud. I suppose you were hoping it might be the twang Of your husband's bow, For why else is the hair on your body bristling?
सहइ सहइ त्ति तेण तहा रमिआ सुरअदुव्विअड्डेण,पव्वाअसिरीसाइ व जह से जाआइ अंगाइं	Because she put up with it all The clumsy youth went on making love to her So that her limbs now look like wilting acacia flowers.
असरिसचित्ते दिअरे सुद्धमणा पिअअमे विसमसीले,ण कहइ कुडुंवविहडणभएण तणुआअए सोण्हा	She does not complain to her husband About his brother's advances Not because she herself has impure thoughts But because he is so touchy And she is afraid of causing a split in the family. Instead she pines away.
चिंताणिअदइअसमागमम्मि कअमण्णुआइ भरिऊण,सुण्णं कलहा अंती सहीहि रुण्णा ण ओहसिआ	Imagining how it was when her lover was with her, The woman suddenly remembered how angry she had been And raged against thin air. Far from laughing, her friends wept for her.
हिअअण्णुएहि समअं असमत्ताइं पि जह सुहावेंति,कज्जाइ मणे ण तहा इअरेहि समाणिआइं पि	Dealings with sympathetic people, Even if inconclusive, Are, I think, more pleasant Than dealings concluded With their opposite.
दरफुडिअसिप्पिसंपुडणिलुक्कहालाहलग्गछेप्पणिहं,पिक्कंवट्ठिविणिग्गअकोमलम् अंवंकुरं उअह	Look! A tender shoot has sprouted from the stone of a ripe mango. It looks like an eel hiding in a half-opened oyster shell.
उअह पडलंतरोइण्णणिअअतंतुद्धपाअपडिलग्गं,दुल्लक्खसुत्तगुत्थेक्कवउलकुसुमं व मक्कडअं	Look at that spider climbing down from the rafters Along a thread spun from between its feet: It looks like a mimosa flower strung on an invisible string.
जइ होसि ण तस्स पिआ अणुदिअहं णीसहेहि अंगेहिं,णवसूअपीअपेओसमत्तपाडि व्व किं सुअसि	If you are not his lover, How come you sleep every day, Your limbs as weak As those of a newborn buffalo calf, Drunk on its mother's milk?
हेमंतिआसु अइदीहरासु राईसु तं सि अविणिद्दा,चिरअरपउत्थवइए ण सुंदरं जं दिआ सुअसि	The winter nights are long, For months your husband's been away, So you must be sleeping well. How odd that you should fall asleep by day.
जइ चिक्खिल्लभउप्पुअपअम् इणम् अलसाइ तुह पए दिण्णं,ता सुहअ कंडइज्जंतम् अंगम् एण्हिं किणो वहसि	If that woman, who stepped on your foot As she leapt away from the mud, Were so indifferent, Why, my dear, is your body now covered With gooseflesh?
पत्तो छणो ण सोहइ अइप्पहाए व्व पुण्णिमाअंदो,अंतविरसो व्व कामो असंपआणो अ परिओसो	Once the festival starts its glamor is over, Like the full moon in broad daylight, Like sex which in the end loses its savor, Or like gratitude without a steady stream of gifts.
पाणिग्गहणे च्चिअ पव्वईअ णाअं सहीहि सोहग्गं,पसुवइणा वासुइकंकणम्मि ओसारिए दूरं	Already at her wedding Paravati's friends knew she would be happy When Siva tossed aside The snake bracelet that frightened her.
गिंहे दवग्गिमसिमइलिआइ दीसंति विंझसिहराइं,आससु पउत्थवइए ण होंति णवपाउसब्भाइं	What you see are the heights of the Vindhya Painted black by the forest fires of summer, Not fresh rain clouds. So do not worry about your husband's return.
जेत्तिअमेत्तं तीरइ णिव्वोढुं देसु तेत्तिअं पणअं,ण जणो विणिअत्तपसाअदुक्खसहणक्खमो सव्वो	Give as much affection As you can muster. For not everyone can bear to suffer The withdrawal of kindness.
वहुवल्लहस्स जा होइ वल्लहा कह वि पंच दिअहाइं,सा किं छट्ठं मग्गइ कत्तो मिट्ठं च वहुअं च	How can a woman Who for five whole days Has been the lover of such an attractive man Ask for one day more? One cannot feast on dainties.
जं जं सो णिज्झाअइ अंगोआसं महं अणिमिसच्छो,पच्छाएमि अ तं तं इच्छामि अ तेण दीसंतं	Whatever part of my body he stares at I cover. At the same time I want him to see it.
दढमण्णुदूमिआइ वि गहिओ दइअम्मि पेछह इमीए,ओसरइ वालुआमुट्ठिओ व्व माणो सुरसुरंतो	See how the woman's indignation at her husband Escapes with a soft sigh Like sand from a clenched fist.
ण वि तह विएसवासो दोग्गच्चं मह जणेइ संतावं,आसंसिअत्थविमुहो जह पणइअणो णिअत्तंतो	More than his absence abroad Or my wretchedness here at home What pains me is my husband returning Without quite reaching his goal.
भरिमो से गहिआहरधुअसीसपहोलिरालआउलिअं,वअणं परिमलतरलिअभमरालिपइण्णकमलं व	I will never forget how she shook her head When I tried to kiss her lips And her tresses flew in all directions. Her face looked like a lotus Surrounded by a swarm of bees Excited by its fragrance.
हल्लफलण्हाणपसाहिआण छणवासरे सवत्तीण,अज्जाइ मज्जणाणाअरेण कहिअं व सोहग्गं	When her rivals take a freezing cold bath Before dressing for the festival, The youngest wife shows her privileged position By not bothering.
ण्हाणहलिद्दाभरिअंतराइ जालाइ जालवलअस्स,सोहंति किलिंचिअकंटएण कं काहिसि कअत्थं	You won't make anyone happy By sitting here Removing with a bamboo needle The traces of turmeric soap From the meshes of your filigree bracelet.
