चंचुपुडाहअविअलिअसहआररसेण सित्तदेहस्स,कीरस्स मग्गलग्गं गंधंधं भमइ भमरउलं	A swarm of bees blindly pursues the parrot Whose feathers are spattered with the juice Dripping from the mango it has pecked with its beak.
एत्थ णिमज्जइ एत्ता एत्थ अहं एत्थ परिअणो सअलो,पंथिअ रत्तीअंधअ मा मह सअणे णिमज्जिहिसि	Here's my mother-in-law's bed, Here is mine, And there those of the servants. Traveler, you won't see in the dark, So do be careful not to fall into mine.
परिओससुंदराइं सुरएसु लहंति जाइ सोक्खाइ,ताइं चिअ उण विरहे खाउग्गिण्णाइ कीरंति	The pleasures of love, Which gave the women such complete delight, Are chewed over and endlessly regurgitated Once their husbands have gone abroad.
मग्गं चिअ अलहंतो हारो पीणुण्णआण थणआण,उव्विग्गो भमइ उरे जमुणाणइफेणपुंजो व्व	Finding no way between her full, upcurving breasts, Her necklace of pearls dances upon her chest Like the bubbles of foam on the Yamunā.
जे जे गुणिणो जे जे अ चाइणो जे विअड्ढविण्णाणा,दारिद्द रे विअक्खण ताण तुमं साणुराओ सि	All the worthy people I meet, All the generous and discerning ones Already receive your favors, You clever devil, Poverty.
जइ कोत्तिओ सि सुंदर सअलतिहीचंददंसणसुहाणं,ता मसिणं मोइज्जंतकंचुअं पेक्खसु मुहं से	Handsome man, If you want to enjoy the sight Of every phase of the moon Look at her gentle face As she slowly lifts her bodice Over her head.
समविसमणिव्विसेसा समंतओ मंदमंदसंचारा,अइरा होहिंति पहा मणोरहाणं पि दुल्लंघा	The lie of the land is blurred And everywhere progress gets slower: Soon the roads will be impassable Even for the wheels of his fancy.
