अत्थक्करूसणं खणपसिज्जणं अलिअवअणणिव्वंधो,उम्मच्छरसंतावो पुत्तअ पअवी सिणेहस्स	Sudden outbursts of anger and the next moment calm, Constant pretence as well as agonies of jealousy, Such, my son, is the nature of love.
अइ उज्जुए ण लज्जसि पुच्छिज्जंती पिअस्स चरिआइं,सव्वंगसुरहिणो मरुवअस्स किं कुसुमरिद्धीहि	You simpleton, Shouldn't you be a little more discreet When people ask how your lover behaves? With all its leaves so fragrant, What need has the marjoram for a mass of blooms?
मुद्धे अपत्तिअंती पवालअंकुरअणिद्धलोहिअए,णिद्धोअधाउराए कीस सहत्थे पुणो धुअसि	Foolish girl, Why are you still washing The red powder from your soft palms That are by nature pink As a spray of coral?
पुससु मुहं ता पुत्तिअ वाहोअरणं विसेसरमणिज्जं,मा एअं चिअ मुहमंडणं ति सो काहिइ पुणो वि	Young girl, Wipe away these tears Which make your face look even more attractive, For he might do it again, Thinking how well they suit you.
अवरण्हागअजामाउअस्स विउणेइ मोहणुक्कंठं,वहुआइ घरपलोहरमज्जणपिसुणो वलअसद्दो	The tinkle of bracelets As she took a bath in the backyard of her parents' house Redoubled the passion of her husband Who had arrived in the late afternoon.
जुज्झचवेडामोडिअजज्जरकण्णस्स जुण्णमल्लस्स,कच्छावंधो च्चिअ भीरुमल्लहिअअं समुक्खणइ	The old wrestler With ears mangled by many a fight Has only to gird up his loins For his fearful opponent to lose heart.
आणंदंतेन तुमं पइणो पहएण पडहसद्देण,मल्लि ण लज्जसि णच्चसि दोहग्गे पाअडिज्जंते	Instead of dancing for joy Should you not feel shame? The drum that celebrates your husband's victory In the wrestling match Makes your unhappy marriage Known to all the world.
मा वच्चह वीसंभं इमाण वहुचाडुअम्मणिउणाणं,णिव्वत्तिअकज्जपरम्मुहाण सुणआण व खलाणं	Don't trust those bastards! They're just like dogs: First they fawn But once they've had their way They turn their backs on you.
सच्चं साहसु देअर तह तह चडुआरएण सुणएण,णिव्वत्तिअकज्जपरम्मुहत्तणं सिक्खिअं कत्तो	Tell me, brother-in-law, That dog who fawned on the bitch So persistently, Where did he learn to turn his back on her The moment he'd had his way?
णिप्पण्णसस्सरिद्धी सच्छंदं गाइ पामरो सरए,दलिअणवसालितंडुलधवलमिअंकासु राईसु	In autumn, when the corn is ripe, The farmer would do as he likes If only the moonlit nights weren't bright As the fresh grains of husked rice.
अलिहिज्जइ पंकअले हलालिचलणेण कलमगोवीए,केआरसोअरुंभणतंसट्ठिअकोमलो चलणो	Bees circle round the rice girl's pink foot Placed across the sluice To stop the water flowing Into the paddy field.
दिअहे दिअहे सूसइ संकेअअभंगवड्ढिआसंका,आवंडुरोणअमुही कलमेण समं कलमगोवी	Just like the rice, Each day her head bends lower And her face grows paler —The girl who guards the paddy, As she grows more fearful of the day When her occupation will cease.
दट्ठूण हरिअदीहं गोसे संढाण जूरए हलिओ,असईरहस्समग्गं तुसारधवले तिलच्छेत्ते	When at dawn he sees a long swathe of green Through the frost-white field of sesame —His faithless wife's clandestine trail— The farmer blames himself for letting loose the bulls.
संकेल्लिओ व्व णिज्जइ खंडं खंडं कओ व्व पीओ व्व,वासागमम्मि मग्गो घरहुत्तमुहेण पहिएण	At the approach of the rains The traveler is so intent on getting home That he bundles up the road and takes it with him, That he cuts it into manageable pieces, That he swallows it down in one gulp.
एण्हिं वारेइ जणो तइआ मूइल्लओ कहिं व गओ,जाहे विसं व जाअं सव्वंगपहोलिरं पेम्मं	Nowadays people restrain me But when this love, Which like a poison courses through all my limbs, First began They were mute.
अण्णोण्णकलक्खंतरपेसिअमेलीणदिट्ठिपसराइं,दो च्चिअ मण्णे कअभंडणाइ समअं पहसिआइं	When their surreptitious glances met The couple whom I thought were sulking Both burst out laughing.
धण्णा वहिरंधरआ ते च्चिअ जीअंति माणुसे लोए,ण सुणंति पिसुणवअणं खलाण अद्धिं ण पेक्खंति	Happy are the deaf and the blind! Though they live among humankind They hear not a single word of slander Nor see how the wicked prosper.
