अव्वो तहिंतहिं चिअ गअणे भमिऊण वीसमंतेण,वोहित्तवाअसेण व्व हासिआ डड्ढपेम्मेण	Who would not love to be tough on a cringing husband But for the long winter nights That erode one's pride?
दे आ दुमसु तुमं चिय मा परिहर पुत्ति पढमदुमियं ति,किं कुड्डं णिअमुहअंदकंतिदुमिअं ण लक्खेसि	O! What a fool Love has made of me, As when the ship's crow Circles the whole heaven Only to settle on the ship again.
विज्जंति तणुं उवणेंति वेअणं णेयताण खयमग्गे,अब्बो अइट्ठपुव्वो अणंगबाणाण माहप्पो	Hey there, daughter— Keep on whitewashing that wall. Don't stop because you think the job's already done. Can't you see? It's the moonlight of your face That makes it look so white.
आमोडऊण बलाउ हत्थं मज्झं गओ सि भो पहिअ,हिअआउ जइ अ णीहसि सामत्थं तुज्झ जाणिस्सं	They pierce one's body, Cause pain But without making wounds. Ah! Love's arrows are unique.
सद्धा मे तुज्झ पियत्तणस्स अहयं तु तं ण याणामि,दे पसिय तुमं चिय सिक्खवेसु जह ते पिया होमि	Having wrenched yourself from my grip You left for the road, But only when you manage to escape from my heart as well Will I acknowledge your power.
पेम्मुम्मइयाइ मए उवऊढो हलियउत्तबुद्धीए,फंसेमि जाव फरुसो तणपुरिसो गामसीमाए	Blind with love I threw my arms around him, Taking him for a farmer's boy. But when I touched him He was just a spiky scarecrow At the village boundary.
बे मग्गा धरणियले माणिणि माणोण्णयाण पुरिसाण,अहवा पावंति सिरिं अहव भमंता समप्पंति	Proud woman, Here on earth two ways are open To people who are proud and haughty: Either they find a treasure Or they are pilgrims of love For the rest of their lives.
कत्तो कमलाण रई कत्तो कुमुयाण सीअलो चंदो,तह सज्जणाण णेहो ण चलइ दूरट्ठिआणं पि	What has the hot sun, Which makes the lotuses unfold, In common with the cool moon Which makes the water lilies unfold? It's as with a good man's affection, Which does not alter However far away he may be.
ढंखरसेसो वि हु महुअरेण मुक्को ण मालईविडवो,दरवियसियकलियामोयबहलिमं संभरंतेण	Though the twigs were completely bare, The bees clung to the jasmine, Savoring the memory of the scent Which burst from the buds that had been there.
डहिऊण सयलरण्णं अग्गी समविसमलंघणुव्वायो,तडलंबंततणेहिं तिसिय व्व णइं समोसरइ	After burning the entire forest The fire was worn out With crossing hill and plain. So, holding on to the grass that grew on the steep bank, It went down to the river for a drink.
रअणायरस्स साहेमि णम्मए अज्ज मुक्कदक्खिण्णा,वेडिसलयाहरंतेण मिलिया जं सि पूरेण	River-nymph Narmadā, Today I will put discretion aside And tell your husband, the sea, How you had a rendezvous with the stream In a bower of reeds.
तिसिया पियउ त्ति मओ मओ वि तिसिओ मई करेऊण,इय मयमिहुणं तिसियं पियइ ण सलिलं सिणेहेण	The stag thought that she was more thirsty than he And the doe thought that he was more thirsty than she. In this way the thirsty couple Out of consideration for each other Did not drink at all!
णिवडिहिसि सुण्णहियए जलहरजलपंकिलम्मि मग्गम्मि,उप्पेक्खागयपिययमहत्थे हत्थं पसारेंती	Watch out! The path is slippery after today's shower. If you grope for the hand of your lover Whom you imagine is standing beside you, You are bound to fall over.
उच्छंगियाऎ पइणा अहिसारणपंकमलिणपेरंते,आसण्णपरियणो विअ सेअ च्चिय धुवइ से पाए	As soon as her husband took her on his lap Sweat poured from her Like an attentive servant, Washing the mud of last night's assignation From her feet.
अणुसोयइ हलियबहू रइकिरणोलुग्गपंडुरच्छायं,रण्णुंदुरदंतुक्खुत्तविसमवलियं तिलच्छेत्तं	The plowman's wife bemoans the sesame field, Bleached by the rays of the sun And pockmarked by the burrowing of field mice.
कमलायराण उण्हो हेमंतो सीअलो जणवयस्स,को किर भिण्णसहावं जाणइ परमत्थयं लोए	Who needs a blanket, Who needs a fire, And who needs a bedchamber, If he has a wife with warm breasts Lying snug against his chest?
पढमं चिय माहवपट्टयं व घेत्तूण डाहिणो वाओ,अंकोल्लपढमवत्तं पहिंडिओ गामरच्छासु	As though seizing the first sign of spring, The south wind whirls the first aṃkolla leaf Through the village streets.
सो माणो पियमुहअंददंसणे कह थिरो धरिज्जिहइ,अंकोल्लकोरआण वि जो फुट्टमुहाण बीहेइ	How is this pride going to stand its ground At the sight of the beloved's face If it is already alarmed By the burgeoning buds of the aṃkolla?
कारणगहिओ वि मए माणो एमेअ जं समोसरियो,अत्थक्कफुल्ल अंकोल्ल तुज्झ तं मत्थए पडउ	That my sulking mood, Which was completely justified, Disappeared just like that, Is entirely your doing, Aṃkolla plant, As you unexpectedly started to blossom
दूरपइण्णपरिमलं सपल्लवं मुद्धपुप्फपंगुरणं,अंगच्छित्तं पिव वम्महेण दिण्णं महुसिरीए	Spring offers her body With its drifting fragrance, Leafspray fingers, And cloak of tender flowers As a playground To the God of Love.
कारणगहिअं पि इमा माणं मोएइ माणिणिअणस्स,सहयारमंजरी पियसहि व्व कण्णे समल्लीणा	This mango bud Hanging from her ear, Like a dear friend whispering good advice, Succeeds in banishing sulkiness, However justified it may be.
अज्जं चिय छणदिअहो मा पुत्ति रुएहि एहइ पिओ त्ति,सुण्हं आसासंती पडियत्तमुही रुवइ सासू	"""My daughter, stop crying. He will come. For he has never before missed today's fair."" With these empty words She reassured her son's wife, Turning her face away To hide her tears."
गुणसालिणो वि करिणो होहइ जूहाहिवत्तणं कत्तो,णवसालिकवललोहिल्लिआऎ विंझं मुअंतस्स	How can an elephant Ever become leader of the herd If he leaves the Vindhya With its wild rice For the sake of a mouthful of rice From a paddy field?
णक्खमऊहेसु खणं कुसुमेसु खणं खणं किसलएसु,हत्थेसु खणं कुसुमोच्चियाइ लोडाविया भसला	One moment the bees are hovering Over the bright fingernails Of the girl picking flowers, The next over the flowers, The next over the shoots, And the next over the girl's hands.
जीहाइ परं लिब्भइ दंतोट्ठेणं ण तीरए गहिउं,अहरो व्व सव्वणो गोहणेण पढमो तणुच्छेओ	Unable to grip the new blade of grass With its teeth or lips, The cow merely licks it with its tongue As one does a bruised lip.
विलासणिगुरुणिअंवो तीरउ चलणेहि दोहि उव्वहिउं,एआई उण मज्झो थणभारं कइ णु उव्वहि	It takes two feet to support the woman's broad hips. So how can her waist on its own Support her heavy breasts?
वारिज्जंती णवकोमुइ त्ति मा पुत्ति अंगणे सुवसु,मा ते अंवुपिसाओ चंदो त्ति मुहं गसिज्जिहिइ	Daughter, be warned: It's a new moon. So do not sleep in the courtyard tonight Lest the moon-eating demon swallow your face by mistake.
सुव्वंतो आसि परंपराइ कहकह वि दिट्ठिमिलिओ ऽसि,दे सुहअ किं पि जंपसु पिअंतु कण्णाइ मे अमिअं	I have heard so much about you from others And now at last I see you with my own eyes. Please, my dear, say something So that my ears, too, may drink nectar.
रोआविअ म्ह माए अंगणपहिएण दरपसुत्तेण,परिवत्तसु माणिणि माणिणि त्ति सिविणे भणंतेण	"Mother, if you ask me what made me cry, It's that traveler dozing in our courtyard Who in his dream pleaded: ""Stop being angry, Please stop being angry and turn over."""
सरहसविणिग्गआइ वि इच्छाइ तुमं ण तीअ सच्चविओ,सीसाहअवलिअभुअंगवंकरच्छे हअग्गामे	Though she ran out quickly She failed to spot you. In this damned village the street twists Like a snake hit on the head.
सा तुह विरहे णिक्किव संधारिज्जइ सहीहि णिउणाहि,चंडालहत्थगअसउणिअ व्व जीए णिरालंवा	In your absence, cruel man, She is as helpless as a bird in the hands of a fowler And is only kept alive by her understanding friends.
अणुराअरअणभरिअं कंचणकलस व्व तरुणिथणवट्टं,तस्स चिअ मुहम्मि किआ मसिमुद्दा मअणराएण	The girl's breasts Are like golden pots filled with the jewels of affection. In the middle of each King Love has set his dark seal.
गाहाण अ गेआण अ तन्तीसद्दाण पोढमहिलाण,ताणं सो च्चिअ दण्डो जे ताण रसं ण आणंति	Poems, songs, the sound of the lute, And impudent women, To men who have no taste for such things They are a punishment.
लडहविलआण लोअणकडक्खविक्खेवजणिअसंदावा,झिज्जंति महासत्ता चित्तुव्वेअणसहा होंति	The pain inflicted by the sidelong glances Of seductive women —Saints suffer it too But they master their emotions.
अव्वो ण आमि छेत्तं खज्जउ साली वि कीरणिवहेहिं,जाणंता अवि पहिआ पुच्छंति पुणोपुणो मग्गं	I won't go to the field. What do I care if the parrots eat all the paddy. Whenever I'm there Travelers keep asking me the way Which they know perfectly well.
अत्थक्कागअदिट्ठे वहुआ जामादुअम्मि गुरुपुरओ,जूरइ णिवडंताणं हरिसविफंदंतवलआणं	Surprised by her husband's arrival At her parents' house, The girl was annoyed with her bracelets For dancing up and down her arms And threatening to slip off.
एह इमीअ णिअच्छह विम्हिअहिअआ सही पुलोएइ,अद्दाअम्मि कवोलं कवोलपट्टम्मि अद्दाअं	How surprised the girl is To see her friend's cheek in the mirror And the mirror in her cheek.
कइआ जाआ कइआ णु सिक्खिआ माइआ हअकुमारी,तंतं जाणइ सव्वं जंजं महिलाऒ जाणंति	How old is she, This damned girl? And when did she learn it all? She already knows everything That a mature woman knows.
खणपिट्ठधूसरत्थणि महुमअतंबच्छि कुवलआभरणे,कण्णगअचूअमंजरि पुत्ति तुए मंडिओ गामो	Young girl, On this day of Holê —Your breasts dusted with flour, Your eyes red from too much liquor, A lotus stuck in your hair And mango shoots behind your ears— You are a credit to our village.
मग्गिअलद्धे बलमोडिचुंबिए अप्पणेण उवणीदे,एक्कम्मि पिआअहरे अण्णण्णा होंति रसहेआ	One time you get them only after a long search, At another you kiss them after a struggle, At yet another they are freely offered —One pair of lover's lips Is an inexhaustible source of delights.
उप्फुल्ललोअणेणं कवोलबोसट्टमाणसेएणं,अहणंतेण वि भणिआ मुहेण से कज्जणिव्वुत्ती	By her wide open eyes, By the sweat streaming down her cheeks, The woman said without saying a word That her part of the business was fulfilled.
जत्थ ण उज्जागरओ जत्थ ण ईसा विसूरणं माणो,सब्भावचाडुअं जत्थ ण त्थि णेहो तहिं ण त्थि	Where there is no wakefulness, Jealousy, strife, sulking, And good old flattery, There no love is either.
मह पइणा थणजुअले पत्तं लिहिअं ति गव्विआ कीस,आलिहइ महं पि पिओ जइ से कंपो च्चिअ ण होइ	Why so proud About your husband having painted a pattern On your breasts? My husband would have done the same If his hand had not trembled so much.
कण्णे पडिअं हिअए पडिअं चिअ ओ मए अभव्वाए,जामि त्ति तुज्झ वअणं किं व ण सहिअं पवासस्स	"They fell on my ear And struck at my heart —Oh what more can I suffer?— Your parting words: ""I'm off."""
समपंथपत्थिअस्स वि पहिअस्स खलंति पुढमदिअहम्मि,हिअअट्ठिअजाआगुरुणिअंवहारेण व पआइ	On the very first day of his journey The traveler stumbled, Though the path was smooth, As if hampered by the heavy buttocks Of the wife he already missed.
संदेसो वि ण लिहिओ लेहे पहिएण कत्थ घरतत्ती,अणवरअलिहिअगेहिणिगोत्तक्खरपूरिए पत्ते	The traveler had written nothing about himself Nor asked how things were at home. The palm leaf was covered all over with the syllables of his wife's name Endlessly repeated.
जह दिअहविरामो णवसिरीसगंधुद्धुराणिलग्घविओ,पहिअघरिणीअ ण तहा तवेइ तिव्वो वि मज्झण्हो	While her husband was abroad The fierce midday sun Did not torment the lonely wife So much as the evening breeze Wafting the scent of fresh acacia blooms.
चिरपवसिअदइअकहा णिउणाहि सहीहि विरहसहणत्थं,अलिआ अवि अवराहा वहूऎ कमसो कहिज्जंति	To help the young wife bear being parted Her ingenious friends tell her tales Of lovers' long absences, Listing the various ways they cause hurt, Some quite imaginary.
जंजं पउत्थपइआ पिअअमणामक्खरं लिहइ लेहे,तंतं तल्लेहणिआणुसारगलिओ पुसइ सेओ	Each time she tries to write a letter To her husband on his travels The drops of sweat running down her pen Blot out the syllables of his dear name.
अच्छउ णिमीलिअच्छी मा मा वारेह पिअअमासाए,तेण विणा किं पेच्छउ उम्मिल्लेहिं वि अच्छीहिं	Let her sit with eyes closed, Dreaming of her husband. For until he returns What is there for her to look at With her eyes open?
जइ देव्व तुं पसण्णो मा करिहिसि मज्झ माणुसं जम्मं,जइ जम्मं मा पेम्मं जइ पेम्मं मा जणे दुलहे	Fate, Please, don't let me be born as a human again. But if it must be, Then don't let me fall in love. But if it must be, Then don't let me fall in love With a man who is so hard to get.
एक्के अअणे दिअहा वीए रअणीऒ होंति दीहाओ,विरहाअणो अपुव्वो एत्थ दुवे च्चेअ वड्ढंति	For half the year the nights are long, For the other half the days. Separation confuses everything As both its days and nights are long.
चिरजीवित्तणकंखिरि मा तम्म रसाअणेहि अथिरेहि,विरहं पवज्ज जाअंति जेण जुअदीहरा दिअहा	If you want to live long Do not trouble about dubious elixirs. Just arrange for your lover to go away, Then the days grow long as eons.
रुअइ रुअंतीऎ मए ओहिदिणे गणइ झिज्जइ अहं व,पिअविरहे मामि सअज्झिआऎ णेहो च्चिअ अपुव्वो	She shares my tears, Counts off each day, And grows as thin as I do While my husband is away. Aunt, the concern my neighbor shows Is quite extraordinary.
कंठग्गहणेण सअज्झिआऎ अब्भागओवआरेण,वहुआऎ पइम्मि वि आगअम्मि सामं मुहं जाअं	As the woman from next door Threw her arms around him To welcome him home, The wife's face grew dark Despite her husband's return.
दूई ण एइ चंदो वि उग्गओ जामिणी वि बोलेइ,सव्वं सव्वत्थो च्चिअ विसंठुलं कस्स किं भणिमो	The messenger is late, The moon is high, And the night is passing. Everything's awry But to whom can I complain?
सो णा ऽगओ त्ति पेच्छह परिहासुल्लाविरीऎ दूईए,णूमंतीअ पहरिसो ओसट्टइ गंडपासेसु	"""He's not coming,"" Teased the go-between. But look: Despite her feigning, A thrill of excitement Steals over her face."
साहेंती सहि सुहअं खणेखणे दूमिआ सि मज्झ कए,सब्भावणेहकरणिज्जसरिसअं दाव विरइअं तुमए	Addressing my lover again and again. Dear friend, all this trouble for my sake. What you do You seem to do out of true love.
जं तुह कज्जं तं चिअ कज्जं मज्झ त्ति जं सआ भणसि,ओ दूइ सच्चवअणे अज्ज सि पारं गआ तस्स	"You always say: ""Your business is my business,"" But today, dear go-between, You've taken it all too literally And gone too far."
णवलअपहरुत्तत्थाऎ तं कअं हलिअवहुआए,जं अज्ज वि जुवइजणो घरेघरे सिक्खिउं महइ	What the young farmer's wife only does After being threatened with a twig Every young maiden In every household Would love to be taught.
पइपुरओ च्चिअ रभसेण चुंबिओ देवरो अडअणाए,मह वअणं मइरागंधिअं ति हाआ तुहं भणइ	Before her husband's eyes The brazen woman passionately kissed his brother's mouth. She said she did so because he'd said That her mouth smelt of drink.
तह अडअणाऎ रुण्णं पइमरणे बाहरुद्धकंठीए,अणुमरणसंकिणो जह जारस्स वि संकिअं हिअअं	The false woman bewailed her dead husband With such choking sobs That even her lover was afraid She might join him on the pyre.
महुएहि किं व वालअ हरसि णिअंबाहि जइ वि मे सिअअं,साहामि कस्स रण्णे दूरे गामो अहं एक्का	Why waste your time with sweetwood flowers, You silly? Just pull the skirt from my hips. Whom can I call to in this wood? The village is a long way off And I am all by myself.
अव्वो कालस्स गई सो वि जुआ सरसकव्वदुल्ललिओ,पढइ परासरसद्दं अम्हे वि णिअं पइं गमिमो	Oh! the passage of time: This young man, Weary of passionate poems, Now studies law While we. . . We stick to our husbands.
भणभण जंजं पडिहाइ तुज्झ तंतं सहामिमो अम्हे,असहत्तणं च जीअं च वल्लभे दोइ ण घडंति	Say what you like: I can take it. For being touchy And living with the man one loves Are two things that don't go together.
एअं चिअ मह णामं भणभण दे सुहअ किं विलक्खो सि,पडिहाइ जं ण तुज्झ वि ममं पि किं देण णामेण	Is that to be my name? Use it, darling, use it: Don't be embarrassed. If my name doesn't appeal to you What use is it to me?
मा वेलवेसु बहुअं पुत्तअ अलिएहि गोत्तेहिं,एसा वि जाणइ च्चिअ परिहासुम्मिस्सभणिआइं	My son, don't overdo That joke of calling her by another woman's name. Your wife also knows how to be funny.
अइ चंडि किं ण पेच्छसि जइ सो वाहरइ अण्णगोत्तेण,अह दे इच्छइ मच्छरपणच्चिअच्छं मुहं दट्ठुं	Hey! you angry girl, Don't you see That when he calls you by the wrong name It's only because he wants to see your eyes Rolling with jealousy?
वेआरिज्जसि मुद्धे गोत्तक्खलिएहि मा खु तुं रुवसु,किं व ण पेच्छइ अण्णह एद्दहमेत्तेहि अच्छीहिं	Foolish girl, you're in a muddle. His getting your name wrong Is nothing to cry about. What do you think? With those big eyes He could never have made such a mistake.
एक्कसअणम्मि सुमुही विमुही गरुएण माणबंधेण,सिविणकलहम्मि होंती परम्मुही सम्मुही जाआ	Wrapped in her feelings of resentment She turned her lovely face away And fell fast asleep on our bed. But continuing the tiff in dream She turned away again And so came face to face with me.
ण वि तह तक्खणसुअमण्णुदुक्खविअणाऒ वि रुवंति,जह दिट्ठम्मि पिअअमे अणुणिज्जंतीऒ तरुणीऒ	The grief and anger they suffer At the moment they hear about their husbands' lapses Do not make young women cry so loud As when the husbands appear in person And ask to be forgiven.
